//! R10 — IS_DEF_EQ_BINDING, native == JIT (Rust -> MIR -> trust-ir ->
//! trust-cg -> machine code): the production binder-congruence OPENS INTO
//! THE CONTEXT. The landed R9 surface (`e2e_ctx_whnf_defeq.rs` — context-
//! aware whnf zeta + proof-irrelevance, untouched as the record) compared
//! Lam-vs-Lam / Pi-vs-Pi by RAW congruence: bodies recursed with loose
//! BVars, never opened. Production is_def_eq_binding
//! (tc/def_eq/binding.rs:12-64, transcribed WHOLE) instead telescopes over
//! consecutive same-kind binders: per binder it pre-checks the domains
//! syntactically (#3230 — production Expr::PartialEq, meta-word filter +
//! derived kind eq), def_eq's them on mismatch, takes a no-loose-bvars fast
//! path (no opening) when neither body mentions the binder, else pushes ONE
//! fresh anonymous FVar (RHS domain + RHS binder-info) and opens BOTH
//! bodies with the SAME id, batch-restoring via ctx_truncate_to
//! (local_context.rs:236-242) on every exit. Call position: quick_is_def_eq
//! (Lam,Lam)|(Pi,Pi) → Some(binding) (def_eq/mod.rs:499-502, consulted at
//! is_def_eq_core entry :300-304 and post-Phase-1 :350-356; Phase-6
//! structural.rs:41-43 routes binder pairs the same way) — the verdict is
//! FINAL both polarities, and proof irrelevance never sees a top-level
//! binder pair (it fires on the OPENED bodies instead). Let never reaches
//! binding (whnf zeta-reduces let-heads — both production and pillar).
//!
//! WHAT IS VERIFIED native==JIT here:
//!   * the R9 20-case decl-gate set RE-RUN through the binding-aware def_eq
//!     (SAME verdicts, payloads deep-compared: REAL-Name payloads
//!     raw-decoded + per-node hash-chain revalidated, expr payloads
//!     meta-bit-identical) PLUS three R10 cases: 20 "def.birrel"
//!     (equality-under-a-binder decided by PROOF IRRELEVANCE OVER THE
//!     OPENED DOMAIN — the opened FVar typed by the context entry BINDING
//!     pushed), 21 "def.bzeta" (a LET pushed OUTSIDE by §7's Let arm
//!     zeta-composes with the binder BINDING opened INSIDE — telescope
//!     iteration 2), 22 "def.alpha" (binder-ATTR differences at both Pi
//!     levels + a redex body: equality unaffected — clean's Lam/Pi carry no
//!     binder names; binding ignores lhs bi, pushes bi2 with Name::anon()).
//!     13 accepts / 10 rejects.
//!   * the binding probes: opening + irrel-under-binder with ctx len
//!     RESTORED and next_id advanced by EXACTLY the telescope pushes
//!     (truncate_to does NOT reset the monotonic counter); the
//!     SHARED-vs-DISTINCT-FVar control (a NON-transcription variant opening
//!     with two fresh ids REJECTS a dependent pair production accepts, and
//!     agrees when the opened var is erased by reduction — the same-id
//!     discipline at binding.rs:49-51 is load-bearing and observable); the
//!     ALPHA meta-word pins (bi-differing Lam and name-differing Let pairs
//!     are meta-BIT-IDENTICAL — compute_meta ignores bi / Let names,
//!     kind.rs:583-586 — while the production syntactic pre-check
//!     expr_syntactic_eq REJECTS both and def_eq accepts); the
//!     POISONED-CONTEXT flip through binding (wrong let VALUE flips the
//!     verdict); REJECT-path cleanup (early truncate) + the ONE infer-only
//!     fallback push; the #3230 pre-check / no-push fast-path observables.
//!   * FALSIFIABILITY — THE BINDING-BLIND CONTROL: `bnd_blind_root` is the
//!     R9-LANDED def_eq configuration kept verbatim (raw binder congruence;
//!     context-aware whnf SHARED; proof-irrel consult intact with its own
//!     self-contained _blind helper chain so the control module contains NO
//!     aware-def_eq/binding body). It runs the SAME 23 cases, itself
//!     native==JIT, AGREES on 0-19 (it ACCEPTS the R9 pair 18/19 — it is
//!     context-aware, ONLY binding-blind) and on 22, and REJECTS exactly
//!     {20, 21} with reject payloads pinned to the un-openable shapes (the
//!     loose BVar #0 vs the proof FVar ĥp̂ under the SAME stuck head Ĉ).
//!   * NEGATIVE CONTROLS: the ARMED module-text corruption (anon seed
//!     `const u64 1723` -> 1724 in the gate module; the case-3 payload
//!     hashes diverge EXACTLY as the production chain predicts); the
//!     poisoned-context flip (probe p3); the distinct-FVar control (p1);
//!     meta-corruption comparator controls.
